faqs:
  - q: What makes this different from a strategy deck?
    a: We stay for the landing. Operating model work has to survive the first re-org, the first quarter-end, and the first real escalation. We build it with the people who will run it.
  - q: How do you avoid workshop fatigue?
    a: Short interviews with the people doing the work. Artifacts that get used after the meeting. We pull what we need and stop taking time.
  - q: How do you measure success?
    a: KPIs agreed before kickoff. Cycle time, cost per transaction, handoff count, error rate, adoption rate. We report against them on the cadence leadership picks.
  - q: Do you handle M&A integrations?
    a: Yes. From day-one readiness to year-one integration. Typical scope 6 to 18 months.
  - q: Who keeps it alive after you leave?
    a: A named internal owner identified early, trained through the project, and handed a plan.
